                <pb facs="0743" n="593" sameAs="frus:frus1907p2/pg593"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 1012/6.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Chargé Brown.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1907-02-28"><hi rendition="#italic">February 28,
                        1907</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 327.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to Mr. Coombs’s No. 516 of the
                    23d ultimo, I inclose a copy of a note from the Chinese minister at Washington,
                    expressing his appreciation of the action of the legation in obtaining redress
                    for a Chinese subject who had been assaulted by a Guatemalan policeman.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. Root.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
